  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5541",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the relationship with NCI-H1693 through multiple pathways, all involving the compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is identified as a target of doxorubicin, and it is also a target of palmarumycin CP18, which further links doxorubicin to NCI-H1693. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin may act through a mechanism involving the inhibition of a purinoceptor, specifically P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by doxorubicin and by palmarumycin CP18. The shared target of doxorubicin and palmarumycin CP18 with NCI-H1693 indicates a potential mechanism of action that could be relevant to the disease. The presence of multiple pathways connecting doxorubicin to NCI-H1693, all involving the same or related targets, supports the hypothesis that the drug may exert its effects through a specific biological mechanism that is relevant to the disease. The integration of these pathways suggests a possible role for the compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate in mediating the interaction between doxorubicin and NCI-H1693.",
